---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/daniel-foster.jpg';
---

<Layout
	title="About me"
	description="Daniel Foster is a data and AI leader in Louisville, Kentucky, writing about data management and putting AI to work on real company data."
>
	<Image
		src={headshot}
		alt="Daniel Foster"
		width={440}
		height={440}
		class="headshot"
		loading="eager"
	/>
	<p>
		I'm Daniel Foster, a data and AI leader based in Louisville, Kentucky. For more than a decade
		I've worked on the same problem from different angles: getting the right data to the people who
		need it, in a form they can trust.
	</p>

	<h2>What I do</h2>
	<p>
		Today I'm a Senior Data Services Manager at SoundHound AI, where I build platforms that let
		business teams answer their own questions with company data. Lately that means connecting large
		language models to the data warehouse through the Model Context Protocol (MCP), so people can ask
		questions in plain English, with guardrails that check every query the AI writes before it runs.
	</p>
	<p>
		Day to day I work across SQL Server, Azure, BigQuery, and Databricks: building pipelines,
		planning migrations, modeling profitability, and moving reporting to tools people actually use.
	</p>

	<h2>How I got here</h2>
	<p>
		I started as an IS intern at Baptist Healthcare in 2013 while finishing a degree in Computer
		Information Systems at the University of Louisville. Since then I've been a programmer/analyst
		and BI team lead at AIG, a SQL Server database administrator at ZirMed (now Waystar), a senior
		BI developer at Republic Bank, a senior data engineer for SharperImage.com, and a data services
		manager at SYNQ3 Restaurant Solutions.
	</p>
	<p>
		That path ran through healthcare, insurance, banking, e-commerce, restaurant technology, and AI.
		The tools kept changing. The fundamentals didn't: know what your data means, make it reliable,
		and put it where people can use it safely.
	</p>

	<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Practical data management:</strong> modeling, data quality, governance, pipelines,
			and migrations, written for people doing the work.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>AI on real data:</strong> what happens when you connect LLMs to company data, what
			works, and how to keep it secure.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Lessons from the field:</strong> what I've learned leading data teams and serving
			business users across very different industries.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Outside of work</h2>
	<p>
		When I'm not working on data projects, my interests include cooking and baking, running,
		coaching my kid's sports teams, and golfing (poorly).
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
		Connect with me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/daniel-foster-04536a75">LinkedIn</a>, or
		follow new posts through the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>.
	</p>

	<p><em>The views on this site are my own and don't represent my employer.</em></p>
</Layout>
<style>
	.headshot {
		float: right;
		width: 220px;
		height: 220px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
		margin: 0.3em 0 1em 1.5em;
		border: 4px solid var(--surface);
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--border);
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.headshot {
			float: none;
			display: block;
			width: 180px;
			height: 180px;
			margin: 0 auto 1.5em;
		}
	}
</style>
